n</italic></sup>'s 					<italic>a</italic> value)                 of the proposed algorithms for finding singleton attractors.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-20180.005" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F6"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Number of iterations done by the proposed algorithms              for <italic>K</italic> = 2.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-20180.006" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F7"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Elapsed time (in seconds) by the proposed algorithms                for random networks with <italic>K</italic> = 2.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-20180.007" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F8"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Elapsed time (in seconds) of some of the proposed             algorithms for random networks with <italic>K</italic> = 2              (Fix) and scale-free networks (PS).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-20180.008" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F9"><label>Algorithm 4</label><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-20180.009" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F10"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Base of the empirical time complexity 					(<italic>a</italic><sup><italic>n</italic></sup>'s 					<italic>a</italic> value)                 of the proposed algorithms for finding cyclic attractors with period 2.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="BSB2007-20180.010" alt-version="no" position="float" xlink:type="simple"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F11"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Base of the empirical time complexity 					(<italic>a</italic><sup><italic>n</italic></sup>'s 					<italic>a</italic> value)               of the proposed algorithms for finding cyclic attractors with period 3.</p></caption><